  "saferAlternatives": [
    "Keep 'Allow write operations' off in P6 MCP Settings (the default): the server then lists no write tool and refuses every write call itself, whatever the client decides.",
    "Every write is a dry run first and applies only with the single-use confirmation token it returns; deleting a project or an activity and restoring a backup also need a confirmation text.",
    "A backup is taken before every write, each write goes to the edit log, and writes are refused while P6 (PM.exe) is running. Open P6 and press F9 after a write.",
    "Use the Basic tool profile (11 read-only tools) or XER-only mode, which loads XER files into a private read-only copy without touching a P6 database."
